prosemirror-view 1.43.0: a key-driven move to the document's start, made within 200 ms of the editor taking focus, is
kept rather than taken for the browser's reset of the selection on focus.

Upstream, DOMObserver.flush restores the state's selection when, within 200 ms of focus, the DOM caret lands at the
document's start with no click or touch in the last 300 ms. It does not look at keys, so Ctrl+Home (Cmd+Up) pressed
just after focusing (leaving a header or note, closing a dialog) is undone. The one added condition,
`view.input.lastKeyCodeTime <= view.input.lastFocus`, lets the check act only when no key was pressed since the focus.
See docs/specs/034-text-documents/editing-surface.md "The caret" and apps/live/e2e/office/caret-after-focus.spec.ts.
Unchanged on upstream master at ca4c78e9b5; drop this patch once an upgrade carries the same condition.

